# Client routes — SCOPED, deliberately. No wildcard `/* /index.html
# 200`: a wildcard makes Cloudflare Pages answer every missing hashed
# asset with index.html as 200 text/html, which strict-MIME refuses and
# the immutable cache header then pins for a year (docs/DEPLOY.md, "The
# 404 contract"). Adding a route in src/Route.elm means adding a line
# here by name, and that friction is the point. CI fails the build if a
# wildcard appears.

/plan /index.html 200
/resources /index.html 200
/legal /index.html 200
